2: Polymorphism
Design and implement a C++ program that demonstrates polymorphism using a suitable real-world example.
Your program should:
Define a parent class with at least one virtual member function.Define at least two derived classes that override the virtual member function.Demonstrate runtime polymorphism by calling the overridden function through a base-class pointer or reference.Create suitable objects and demonstrate how the same function call produces different behaviours depending on the object.Use hand drawn illustrations to explain polymorphism.
